{"id":"cable_crossover","name":"Cable crossover","cue":"Lean in, elbows soft, sweep your hands down and together.","research":"Standing high-pulley cable crossover, both pulleys above head height (1.10 H, 1.96 m; York lists 82 in overall height) 0.56 H (1.0 m) either side of the stance (2.0 m between the pulleys) and slightly behind it. Staggered stance (left foot 0.18 H forward, both soles flat), trunk leaned 18 deg from vertical with the hinge at the hips (pelvis 12, lumbar 3, thorax 3), knees soft (front 15, back 0). The standard technique description, not a measured trial: hands start wide at shoulder height with the elbows soft (shoulder elevation 84, horizontal abduction just behind the frontal plane, elbow 18) and sweep down and together to the front of the hips (elevation 42, plane 100 past straight ahead, elbow 22), the humerus never passing the shoulder line. Scapulae retracted at the stretch (clavicle pro -8) and protracted at the end (+8). Stirrup handles ride on the fists (a free-swinging triangle on the grip bar that follows the cable, dswing); the hand pronates from 50 to 90 so the bar stays square to the cable. Cable 1:1 to the stack. Geometry: design/cable/cx.mjs.","targets":{"tol":10,"A":{"trunk_flexion":18,"shoulder_elevation":84,"shoulder_plane":-16,"elbow_flexion":18,"hip_flexion_l":29,"knee_flexion_l":15},"B":{"trunk_flexion":18,"shoulder_elevation":42,"shoulder_plane":100,"elbow_flexion":22},"note":"design values (standard technique), not a measured trial: the plane read-back is thorax-relative, the 18 deg forward lean is in the trunk"},"muscles":{"primary":["pec_stern"],"secondary":["delt_ant"],"side":"both"},"camera":{"az":20,"el":18,"dAz":0,"dEl":0,"fill":0.6,"note":"Front three-quarter view (az 20, el 18, 27 deg off the front view): the chest faces the camera on the forward lean, the raised higher lens looks onto the pecs as the hands sweep down and in, and the stagger of the legs still reads. The towers crop at the edges; the cables still